ENTRY            D4441   20260521   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D4441001   20260521   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 10         34
TITLE      Nonresonant capture cross section measurement of the
           29Si(p,gamma)30P reaction
AUTHOR     (Zs.Matyus,L.Csedreki,Zs.Fulop,Z.Halasz,G.G.Kiss,
           T.Szucs,A.Toth,Gy.Gyurky)
INSTITUTE  (3HUNDEB,3HUNKOS)
REFERENCE  (J,JP/G,52,105201,2025)
           #doi:10.1088/1361-6471/ae06bd
FACILITY   (VDGT,3HUNDEB)
SAMPLE     Highly enriched (99.34%) 29Si was evaporated onto
           0.5 mm high-purity Ta sheets. Areal density of 29Si in
           different targets: 1.0027E18 atoms/cm2
                              0.919E18 atoms/cm2
                              0.987E18 atoms/cm2
DETECTOR   (HPGE)
METHOD     (ACTIV) Direct capture cross section was measured by
           using charged particle activation method.
           (GSPEC) Activity measurement of the reaction products
           was done by gamma ray spectrometry.
ERR-ANALYS (EN-ERR)
           The total uncertainty of the energy values is estimated
           using the standard method, which involves taking the
           quadratic sum of the independently contributing
           parameters: beam energy (0.1 keV), half energy
           loss in targets (5.5-7.5 keV).
           (ERR-T)
           The total uncertainty of the cross-section values is
           estimated using the standard method, which involves
           taking the quadratic sum of the independently
           contributing parameters including the statistical and
           systematic uncertainties.
           (ERR-1) beam intensity (3%)
           (ERR-2) detection efficiency (3%)
           (ERR-3) implantation probability calculation (7.5%)
HISTORY    (20260521C)         TT
ENDBIB              34
COMMON               3          3
